  "question_stem": "A particle $P$ moving in a straight line starts from rest at a point $O$ and comes to rest 16 s later. At time $t$ s after leaving $O$, the acceleration $a$ m s$^{-2}$ of $P$ is given by\n$$a = 6 + 4t \\qquad 0 \\le t < 2,$$\n$$a = 14 \\qquad 2 \\le t < 4,$$\n$$a = 16 - 2t \\qquad 4 \\le t \\le 16.$$\nThere is no sudden change in velocity at any instant.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$t=5$ s and $t=11$ s.",
    "A positive quadratic curve from $(0,0)$ to the given line at $t=2$, and a negative quadratic curve from the given line at $t=4$ to $(16,0)$ with one maximum and no point of inflexion."
  ],
